  // BX-01's tiny science-fiction expedition (BX-01, doc/architecture/mission-22/boundary-brief.md): an orbital station, a
  // shuttle run to a planet, its surface and a dead survey outpost, a problem that matters, and a return to report and
  // trade. Two nested scales (the system and the station or the planet; the planet's surface and the outpost) and one
  // journey: the platform's own passages, travel and actions. Nothing here names Westernesse's catalog but what the
  // platform will not run without, and each such thing is a finding in the report.
  Place system "the Tethys system" is region.
  Place halcyon "Halcyon Station" is settlement within system.
  Place dock "Halcyon's docking ring" is room within halcyon at 0, 0 indoors.
  Place concourse "the station concourse" is room within halcyon at 1, 0 indoors.
  Place ops "station operations" is room within halcyon at 2, 0 indoors.
  Place surface "the surface of Tethys IV" is wilderness within system.
  Place pad "the landing pad on Tethys IV" is room within surface at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place outpost "the survey outpost" is site within surface.
  Place airlock "the outpost airlock" is room within outpost at 0, 0 indoors.
  Place lab "the outpost laboratory" is room within outpost at 1, 0 indoors.
  Passage ring "the ring corridor" is path between dock and concourse.
  Passage lift "the ops lift" is path between concourse and ops.
  Passage shuttle "the shuttle run to Tethys IV" is road between dock and pad taking 6 hours.
  Passage approach "the approach to the outpost" is path between pad and airlock.
  Passage inner "the inner hatch" is door between airlock and lab.
  Company party "You" of 1 at dock.

  // What the company can do here that no fantasy company can: read a dead machine, and bring it back.
  Entity systems: capability "Systems".
  Relation powered(place). Relation reported(group).
  Entity outpost_dark: fact "The survey outpost on Tethys IV has been silent for nine days.".
  Entity beacon_found: fact "The outpost's core logged a seismic fault under the colony site before it went dark.".
  Initially Assert established(outpost_dark). Initially Assert knows(party, outpost_dark).
  Person chief "Chief Okafor" at ops { Role "the station's operations chief". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. }
  Person broker "Ilse Varga" at concourse { Role "a data broker". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. }
  Objective outpost when knows(party, outpost_dark) and not knows(party, beacon_found) toward lab "Find out why the survey outpost on Tethys IV went silent.".
  Objective report when knows(party, beacon_found) and not reported(party) toward chief "Report the seismic fault to Chief Okafor at station operations.".
  Observe lab_dark at lab when not powered(lab) "The lab is dark but for the red standby light on the core, and frost on the inside of the glass.".
  Action restart_core(actor: group, site: place) "Bring the outpost's core back up" {
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lab) and not powered(lab).
    Time 3. Resolve check(actor, mending, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert powered(lab). Assert knows(actor, beacon_found). }
    Result "The core hums, and its log scrolls: a seismic fault, opening under the colony site.".
    Otherwise "The core will not take the restart.".
  }
  Topic report_fault with chief "Tell Chief Okafor what the outpost's core logged" when knows(actor, beacon_found) and not reported(actor) once {
    Says "Okafor reads the log twice. 'We were going to land four hundred people on that,' she says. She authorizes your fee.".
    On discuss { Assert reported(actor). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 40. }
  }
  Kind core_log_kind "a copy of the outpost's log" is document worth 25 weighing 0 described "A data wafer with the outpost's last nine days on it.".
  Topic sell_log with broker "Sell Ilse Varga a copy of the outpost's log" when knows(actor, beacon_found) once {
    Says "Varga pays without haggling, which tells you what it is worth.".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 25. }
  }
  Goal false.
